3. ETHICAL USAGE & PHARMACEUTICAL SAFETY POLICY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This Software is designed exclusively for the safe, transparent, and regulated
redistribution of surplus medicines. Any deployment of this Software must adhere
to the following strict safety principles:

  (a) No Expired Medications: Under no circumstances may this Software be used
      to catalog, approve, or redistribute pharmaceuticals with less than 30 days
      of remaining shelf-life.
  (b) Mandatory Professional Verification: No medicine may be transferred without
      prior physical inspection and digital sign-off by a licensed pharmacist.
  (c) Prohibition of Controlled Narcotics: The Software must not be used for the
      unlicensed exchange of Schedule X, narcotic, or habit-forming substances.
  (d) Sealed Packaging Requirement: Loose tablets, opened syrups, unsealed bottles,
      and compromised foils are strictly prohibited from redistribution.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. STATUTORY & HEALTHCARE REGULATORY COMPLIANCE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MediBridge is an academic research and technology demonstration platform.
The Software is NOT certified as a medical device by any statutory authority.

All physical redistribution operations conducted through or facilitated by this
Software must strictly comply with applicable health statutes, including:
  - The Drugs and Cosmetics Act, 1940 (India)
  - The Drugs and Cosmetics Rules, 1945 (India)
  - Guidelines issued by the Central Drugs Standard Control Organisation (CDSCO)
  - Applicable state and local pharmacy council regulations.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. PRIVACY & DATA INTEGRITY OBLIGATIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Deployers of this Software must maintain strict privacy safeguards:
  - Personal Identifiable Information (PII) of donors must remain redacted.
  - Camera EXIF GPS coordinates must be purged before image storage.
  - The cryptographic integrity of the SHA-256 custody ledger must be maintained.

